dritic arbor, and has dendrites in layers 2 and 5.\")\n21454:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003036 \"M7 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21455:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003036 obo:CL_0000740)\n21459:# Class: obo:CL_0003037 (M7-ON retinal ganglion cell)\n21461:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003037 \"An M7 retinal ganglion cells with synaptic terminals in S4 and is depolarized by illumination of its receptive field center.\")\n21466:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003037 \"M7-ON retinal ganglion cell\")\n21471:# Class: obo:CL_0003038 (M7-OFF retinal ganglion cell)\n21473:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003038 \"An M7 retinal ganglion cells with synaptic terminals in S2 and is depolarized by decreased illumination of their receptive field center\")\n21478:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003038 \"M7-OFF retinal ganglion cell\")\n21483:# Class: obo:CL_0003039 (M8 retinal ganglion cell)\n21485:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003039 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with large soma and medium dendritic field, with dense dendritic arbor.\")\n21490:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003039 \"M8 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21491:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003039 obo:CL_0000740)\n21495:# Class: obo:CL_0003040 (M9 retinal ganglion cell)\n21497:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003040 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with large soma and large dendritic field, with medium dendritic arbor, and has dendrites in layers 1 and 5.\")\n21502:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003040 \"M9 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21503:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003040 obo:CL_0000740)\n21507:# Class: obo:CL_0003041 (M9-ON retinal ganglion cell)\n21509:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003041 \"An M9 retinal ganglion cells with synaptic terminals in S2 and is depolarized by illumination of its receptive field center.\")\n21514:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003041 \"M9-ON retinal ganglion cell\")\n21519:# Class: obo:CL_0003042 (M9-OFF retinal ganglion cell)\n21521:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003042 \"An M9 retinal ganglion cell with synaptic terminals in S4 that is depolarized by decreased illumination of their receptive field center\")\n21526:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003042 \"M9-OFF retinal ganglion cell\")\n21531:# Class: obo:CL_0003043 (M10 retinal ganglion cell)\n21533:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003043 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with large soma and large dendritic field, with dense dendritic arbor.\")\n21538:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003043 \"M10 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21539:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003043 obo:CL_0000740)\n21543:# Class: obo:CL_0003044 (M11 retinal ganglion cell)\n21550:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003044 \"M11 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21551:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003044 obo:CL_0000740)\n21557:# Class: obo:CL_0003045 (M12 retinal ganglion cell)\n21564:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003045 \"M12 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21565:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003045 obo:CL_0000740)\n21571:# Class: obo:CL_0003046 (M13 retinal ganglion cell)\n21573:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003046 \"A bistratifed retinal ganglion cell that has small, symmetric dendritic fields that terminate in S2 and S4.\")\n21578:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003046 \"M13 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21579:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003046 obo:CL_0000740)\n21585:# Class: obo:CL_0003047 (M14 retinal ganglion cell)\n21587:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003047 \"A bistratifed retinal ganglion cell that has small, symmetric dendritic fields that terminate in S1 and S4-S5.\")\n21592:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003047 \"M14 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21593:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003047 obo:CL_0000740)\n21666:# Class: obo:CL_0004115 (retinal ganglion cell B)\n21668:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004115 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with small to medium soma and small to medium dendritic field.\")\n21673:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004115 \"retinal ganglion cell B\")\n21674:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0004115 obo:CL_0000740)\n21678:# Class: obo:CL_0004116 (retinal ganglion cell C)\n21680:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004116 \"A retinal ganglion with cell medium cell bodies and medium to large dendritic fields.\")\n21686:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004116 \"retinal ganglion cell C\")\n21687:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0004116 obo:CL_0000740)\n21690:# Class: obo:CL_0004117 (retinal ganglion cell A)\n21692:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004117 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with large soma and large dendritic field.\")\n21700:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004117 \"retinal ganglion cell A\")\n21701:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0004117 obo:CL_0000740)\n21705:# Class: obo:CL_0004119 (retinal ganglion cell B1)\n21707:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004119 \"A retinal ganglion cell B that has medium body size, medium dendritic field and dense dendritic arbor, and has post synaptic terminals in S2.\")\n21711:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0004119 \"retinal ganglion cell B4\")\n21715:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004119 \"retinal ganglion cell B1\")\n21719:# Class: obo:CL_0004120 (retinal ganglion cell A1)\n21721:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004120 \"A retinal ganglion A cell found in the retina with large somata, often polygonal in shape. The dendritic fields consist of three to seven stout dendrites that are sparce near soma. Dendrites terminate in S4.\")\n21726:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0004120 \"inner alpha retinal ganglion cell\")\n21730:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004120 \"retinal ganglion cell A1\")\n21734:# Class: obo:CL_0004121 (retinal ganglion cell B2)\n21736:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004121 \"A retinal ganglion cell B that has a very small but very dense dendritic field, and has post synaptic terminals in S2.\")\n21742:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004121 \"retinal ganglion cell B2\")\n21746:# Class: obo:CL_0004124 (retinal ganglion cell C1)\n21748:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004124 \"A retinal ganglion cell C inner that has medium dendritic diversity.\")\n21757:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004124 \"retinal ganglion cell C1\")\n21760:# Class: obo:CL_0004125 (retinal ganglion cell C2 inner)\n21762:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004125 \"A retinal ganglion cell C inner that has dense dendritic diversity.\")\n21768:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004125 \"retinal ganglion cell C2 inner\")\n21771:# Class: obo:CL_0004126 (retinal ganglion cell C2 outer)\n21773:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004126 \"A retinal ganglion cell C outer that has symmetrical and dense dendritic dendritic tree with a large dendritic field.\")\n21779:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004126 \"retinal ganglion cell C2 outer\")\n21782:# Class: obo:CL_0004137 (retinal ganglion cell A2 inner)\n21784:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004137 \"A retinal ganglion A2 cell with dendrites terminating in S4.\")\n21790:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004137 \"retinal ganglion cell A2 inner\")\n21794:# Class: obo:CL_0004138 (retinal ganglion cell A2)\n21796:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004138 \"A retinal ganglion A cell with dense arbor near soma.\")\n21799:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0004138 \"outer alpha retinal ganglion cell\")\n21804:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004138 \"retinal ganglion cell A2\")\n21807:# Class: obo:CL_0004139 (retinal ganglion cell A2 outer)\n21809:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004139 \"A retinal ganglion A2 cell with dendrites terminating in S2.\")\n21815:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004139 \"retinal ganglion cell A2 outer\")\n21842:# Class: obo:CL_0004183 (retinal ganglion cell B3)\n21844:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004183 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with medium soma, sparse dendritic tree, and medium dendritic field.\")\n21851:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004183 \"retinal ganglion cell B3\")\n25534:# Class: obo:CL_0020014 (intrinsically photosensitive retinal ganglion cell)\n25536:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11834834\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20959623\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Intrinsically_photosensitive_retinal_ganglion_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020014 \"A retinal ganglion cell that is intrinsically photosensitive, functioning as a non-image-forming photoreceptor, distinguished from rod and cone photoreceptors by the expression of the photopigment melanopsin in mice and humans (Hattar et al., 2002; Tri Hoang Do & Yau, 2015). Located primarily in the ganglion cell layer with some displaced somata in the inner nuclear layer, this neuron depolarises directly in response to environmental irradiance (Tri Hoang Do & Yau, 2015). It projects via the retinohypothalamic tract to central targets, including the suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN) for circadian photoentrainment and the olivary pretectal nucleus (OPN) for the pupillary light reflex.\")\n25542:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020014 \"intrinsically photosensitive retinal ganglion cell\")\n25544:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020014 obo:CL_0000740)\n25649:# Class: obo:CL_0020024 (alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-sustained (Mmus))\n25651:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020024 \"A mouse retinal ganglion cell type defined by a large soma and a wide, monostratified dendritic arbor that stratifies just distal to the outer ChAT band of the inner plexiform layer (Krieger et al., 2017). It corresponds to the G5 physiological type (Baden et al., 2016; Goetz et al., 2022) and the C42 transcriptomic cluster (Tran et al., 2019), and is considered the evolutionary ortholog of the primate OFF midget RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). The cell projects a thick, fast-conducting axon to the dorsal lateral geniculate nucleus and superior colliculus. It shows a sustained increase in firing to light decrements with a slow decay time constant of roughly 250 ms and a large receptive field center with weak surround antagonism (Krieger et al., 2017). Its molecular profile includes expression of Spp1 and Neurofilament (Smi32) together with Brn3a (Pou4f1) and Brn3b (Pou4f2), absence of Brn3c (Pou4f3) and Calbindin (Calb1), and strong enrichment of Fes (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019).\")\n25657:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020024 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-s\")\n25658:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020024 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\n25659:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020024 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-sustained (Mmus)\")\n25664:# Class: obo:CL_0020025 (alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-sustained (Mmus))\n25666:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38092908\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020025 \"A retinal ganglion cell type that has a large soma and a wide, monostratified dendritic arbor that stratifies in the inner sublamina of the inner plexiform layer, with dendrites located just proximal to the inner ChAT band (Krieger et al., 2017). It shows a sustained increase in firing rate to ON stimuli (Krieger et al., 2017). It corresponds to the G24 functional type (Baden et al., 2016; Goetz et al., 2022), the C43 transcriptomic cluster (Tran et al., 2019), and is considered the mouse ortholog of the primate ON midget retinal ganglion cell (Hahn et al., 2023). It is molecularly defined by expression of Spp1, Smi32, Brn3b, Calbindin, and Tbr2 (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019).\")\n25672:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020025 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-s\")\n25673:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020025 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\n25674:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020025 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-sustained (Mmus)\")\n25679:# Class: obo:CL_0020026 (alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-transient (Mmus))\n25681:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020026 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype found in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to decreases in light intensity. It is characterized by a large soma, a broad dendritic arbor that stratifies within sublamina a of the inner plexiform layer, and rapid OFF-transient firing kinetics that decay even during sustained stimulation (Krieger et al., 2017). Functionally, it corresponds to G8 in the Baden functional classification (Baden et al., 2016; Goetz et al., 2022) and C45 in the Tran transcriptomic atlas (Tran et al., 2019), and it is considered the evolutionary ortholog of the primate OFF Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). This cell type acts as a detector of rapidly approaching dark objects and contributes to innate defensive responses by encoding looming stimuli (Münch et al., 2009). It exhibits a distinctive molecular signature by its expression of Brn3c (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\n25686:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020026 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-t\")\n25687:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020026 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\n25688:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020026 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-transient (Mmus)\")\n25693:# Class: obo:CL_0020027 (alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-transient (Mmus))\n25695:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020027 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to increases in light intensity. It possesses the large soma and expansive dendritic field characteristic of alpha RGCs (Krieger et al., 2017). This cell exhibits a brief, fast-decaying burst of firing at the onset of light increments and contributes to motion detection for luminance increases, forming the ON-branch of the transient magnocellular-like pathway (Krieger et al., 2017; Hahn et al., 2023). Functionally, it corresponds to cluster G19 and aligns transcriptomically with cluster C41 (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019). It is orthologous to the primate ON Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). Molecularly, it expresses Spp1, Smi32, and Brn3b, but lacks Brn3a, Brn3c, and Calbindin (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\n25700:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"C41\")\n25702:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-t\")\n25703:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020027 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\n25704:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020027 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-transient (Mmus)\")\n29512:# Class: obo:CL_2000050 (obsolete retina retinal ganglion cell)\n29514:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:TermGenie\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000050 \"Any retinal ganglion cell that is part of a retina.\")\n29519:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_2000050 \"obsolete retina retinal ganglion cell\")\n30435:# Class: obo:CL_4023032 (ON retinal ganglion cell)\n30438:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19602302\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023032 \"A retinal ganglion cell that is depolarized by illumination of its receptive field center.\")\n30439:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023032 \"ON retinal ganglion cell\")\n30440:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023032 obo:CL_0000740)\n30442:# Class: obo:CL_4023033 (OFF retinal ganglion cell)\n30444:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19602302\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023033 \"A retinal ganglion cell that is depolarized by decreased illumination of their receptive field center.\")\n30446:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023033 \"OFF retinal ganglion cell\")\n30447:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023033 obo:CL_0000740)\n31486:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32533915\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Midget_cell&oldid=982299713\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023188 \"A retinal ganglion cell that originate in the ganglion cell layer of the retina, and project to the parvocellular layers of the lateral geniculate nucleus (LGN). These cells are known as midget retinal ganglion cells due to the small sizes of their dendritic trees and cell bodies.\")\n31492:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023188 obo:CL_0000740)\n31495:# Class: obo:CL_4023189 (parasol ganglion cell of retina)\n31497:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32533915\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Parasol_cell&oldid=1032171532\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023189 \"A retinal ganglion cell located in the ganglion cell layer of the retina. This cell projects to magnocellular cells in the lateral geniculate nucleus (LGN). They have large cell bodies and extensive, branching dendritic networks that contribute to their large receptive fields.\")\n31502:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023189 \"These cells should not be confused with M1-M14 retinal ganglion cells described in PMID:16626866 which refer to a different classification of retinal ganglion cells.\")\n31503:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023189 \"parasol ganglion cell of retina\")\n31504:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023189 obo:CL_0000740)\n32572:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22006647\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033027 \"In primates, a diffuse bipolar 1 cell on average makes 81 ribbon (output) synapses, 13 contacts are with OFF parasol cells and 47 contacts are with OFF midget cells. This cell might make flat contacts at both triad-associated and non-triad-associated positions on the cone pedicle.\")\n32578:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25309346\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26500507\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033028 \"An OFF diffuse bipolar cell that predominantly connects to ON parasol cells and lateral amacrine cells. This cell contains a large number of synaptic ribbons and a small axon arbor area.\")\n32582:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033028 \"In primates, a diffuse bipolar 2 cell makes an average of 133 ribbon synapses, 47 contacts are with OFF parasol cells and 4 contacts are with OFF midget cells.\")\n32593:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.3389/fnana.2015.00122\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033029 \"Originally, DB3a cells were termed diffuse bipolar 3 (DB3) cells. When an additional bipolar type which stratifies slightly more vitread and is calbindin negative was detected, this cell was renamed diffuse bipolar 3a cell. The axons of neighboring DB3a cells make homologous gap junctions. The DB3a cells provide the majority of their output to OFF parasol cells.\")\n32609:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32555229\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033031 \"An ON diffuse bipolar cell that predominantly connects to ON parasol cells and lateral amacrine cells.\")\n32820:# Class: obo:CL_4033051 (OFF parasol ganglion cell)\n32822:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033051 \"A parasol ganglion cell that depolarizes in response to decreased light intensity in the center of its receptive field. The majority of input that this cell receives comes from DB3a bipolar cells.\")\n32825:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033051 \"OFF-parasol RGC\")\n32826:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033051 \"OFF-parasol retinal ganglion cell\")\n32827:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033051 \"outer parasol cell\")\n32828:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033051 \"OFF parasol ganglion cell\")\n32831:# Class: obo:CL_4033052 (ON parasol ganglion cell)\n32833:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033052 \"A parasol ganglion cell that depolarizes in response to increased light intensity in the center of its receptive field. The majority of input that this cell receives comes from DB4 bipolar cells.\")\n32836:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033052 \"ON-parasol RGC\")\n32837:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033052 \"ON-parasol retinal ganglion cell\")\n32838:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033052 \"inner parasol cell\")\n32839:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033052 \"ON parasol ganglion cell\")\n32842:# Class: obo:CL_4033053 (small bistratified retinal ganglion cell)\n32844:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033053 \"A bistratfied retinal ganglion cell with a small dendritic field that has dendrites in the ON and OFF sublamina of the retinal inner plexiform layer and carries blue-ON/yellow-OFF signals. This cell receives bipolar and amacrine input to both the OFF and ON dendritic tree.\")\n32852:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified retinal ganglion cell\")\n33066:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033085 \"An ON diffuse bipolar cell that stratifies in the stratum 3 of the inner plexiform layer to make synapses with ON parasol ganglion cells. A diffuse bipolar 5 cell has high expression of MYO16 compared with other bipolar cells.\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
