a that responds selectively and transiently to increases in light intensity. It possesses the large soma and expansive dendritic field characteristic of alpha RGCs (Krieger et al., 2017). This cell exhibits a brief, fast-decaying burst of firing at the onset of light increments and contributes to motion detection for luminance increases, forming the ON-branch of the transient magnocellular-like pathway (Krieger et al., 2017; Hahn et al., 2023). Functionally, it corresponds to cluster G19 and aligns transcriptomically with cluster C41 (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019). It is orthologous to the primate ON Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). Molecularly, it expresses Spp1, Smi32, and Brn3b, but lacks Brn3a, Brn3c, and Calbindin (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\n25696-AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_0020027 obo:NCBITaxon_10090)\n25697-AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020027 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n25698-AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020027 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n25699-AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020027 \"2025-12-05T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n25700-AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"C41\")\n25701-AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"G19\")\n--\n31487-AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023188 \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596\")\n31488-AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023188 \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\")\n31489-AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023188 \"There are midget bipolar cells of retina and midget ganglion cells of retina and they are not the same:\n31490-Midget bipolar cells (imb, fmb) have larger axon terminals at greater distances from the fovea (retinal eccentricity of 4.5mm as compared to 12 mm). Midget ganglion cells (MGC) have larger dendritic fields (here seen at 8 mm) as they increase in eccentricity.\")\n31491-AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023188 \"midget ganglion cell of retina\")\n31492-SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023188 obo:CL_0000740)\n31493-SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023188 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0013001 obo:UBERON_0013607))\n31494-\n31495:# Class: obo:CL_4023189 (parasol ganglion cell of retina)\n31496-\n31497-AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32533915\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Parasol_cell&oldid=1032171532\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023189 \"A retinal ganglion cell located in the ganglion cell layer of the retina. This cell projects to magnocellular cells in the lateral geniculate nucleus (LGN). They have large cell bodies and extensive, branching dendritic networks that contribute to their large receptive fields.\")\n31498-AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023189 \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596\")\n31499-AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023189 \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\")\n31500-AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023189 \"M cell\")\n31501-AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023189 \"M ganglion cell\")\n31502-AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023189 \"These cells should not be confused with M1-M14 retinal ganglion cells described in PMID:16626866 which refer to a different classification of retinal ganglion cells.\")\n31503-AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023189 \"parasol ganglion cell of retina\")\n--\n32823-AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033051 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32824-AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033051 \"2023-08-08T12:34:57Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32825-AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033051 \"OFF-parasol RGC\")\n32826-AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033051 \"OFF-parasol reti